@model ReformedHistory.Views.Content.Confessions.Secret.SecretSection

<h2 id="@this.Model.Link">Chapter @this.Model.Index</h2>
<h3>@this.Model.Name</h3>
<br />

<div class="centerQuote">
    <span>
        In baptism, we are enlisted in the holy military service of Christ, that all 
        our life long we should fight against the world, Satan, and our own flesh
    </span>
    <span>Heinrich Bullinger, The Second Helvetic Confession</span>
</div>

<ol>
    <li>
        Baptism enters, receives, and seals a person in the catholic church and as a member of new covenant 
        @*<a href="#@(this.Model.Link).Sources.1">(@(this.Model.Index).1)</a>*@, which
        is the kingdom of the Lord Jesus Christ and the house and family of God.
        @*<a href="#@(this.Model.Link).Sources.2">(@(this.Model.Index).2)</a>*@
    </li>
    <li>
        Through baptism,
        a person is united to Christ's death and resurrection, is cleansed of their sins by the blood of Lamb, and is
        placed into the regeneration of the Holy Spirit to live a new life of godliness.
        @*<a href="#@(this.Model.Link).Sources.3">(@(this.Model.Index).3)</a>*@
    </li>
    @*<li>
        All of these great gifts are wrought not by the water, but by the Holy Spirit which the water signifies 
        <a href="#@(this.Model.Link).Sources.4">(@(this.Model.Index).4)</a>.
        Nonetheless, the water and the Spirit are sacramentally united by the promises of God, so that as we
        administer the water we are undoubtably assured that the Spirit is truly present 
        <a href="#@(this.Model.Link).Sources.5">(@(this.Model.Index).5)</a>.
    </li>*@
    <li>
        The regenerating work of the Spirit in baptism is received and made effectual only by faith, so 
        that without faith the grace given in baptism falls on rocky ground, and profits a person nothing.
        @*<a href="#@(this.Model.Link).Sources.6">(@(this.Model.Index).6)</a>*@
    </li>
    <li>
        The Spirit's work in the baptized person is not limited to only the moment of administration, but continues
        and grows in the person throughout their entire Christian life. 
    </li>
    <li>
        Though the Holy Spirit has promised to work through baptism, He is not constrained by it. 
        God may save a person in any way He so elects, whether apart from baptism or before its 
        administration. @*<a href="#@(this.Model.Link).Sources.8">(@(this.Model.Index).7)</a>*@
    </li>
    <li>
        Baptism is to be performed in the trinitarian name of the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit. A person is
        only to baptized once in their life, for the new birth cannot be repeated nor revoked.
    </li>
</ol>
<br />

@*<h4>We Deny</h4>
<ul>
    <li>That baptism is a "work of the law"</li>
    <li>That baptism is made effectual by performance of the rite, and not by the Spirit</li>
    <li>That all who are baptized are saved</li>
</ul>
<br />
<br />*@